@startuml bedrock_block
title K9-AIF with AWS Bedrock AgentCore: where each piece sits
top to bottom direction

rectangle "Client / event source" as Client

rectangle "AgentCore Runtime (Path A: hosting)" as RT {
  rectangle "K9-AIF Router\n(admit: authenticate, route by event_type)" as Router

  rectangle "Native K9-AIF path" as Native {
    rectangle "Orchestrator\n(BaseOrchestrator)" as Orch
    rectangle "Squad\n(BaseSquad, YAML flow)" as Squad
    rectangle "Agents\n(BaseAgent, llm_invoke)" as Agents
  }

  rectangle "AgentCore path (Path B)" as PB {
    rectangle "BedrockAgentCoreOrchestratorAdapter\n(is an Orchestrator: BaseOrchestrator + BaseAdapter)" as Adapter
    rectangle "AgentCore Harness\n(managed agent loop)\nor a deployed agent" as Harness
  }
}

rectangle "Shared K9-AIF services (same config for both paths)" as Shared {
  rectangle "Shield governance\n(ingress, egress,\ntool args, tool results)" as Shield
  rectangle "Tool gate\n(registry, record checks,\nrules -> allow / deny / hil)" as Gate
  rectangle "HIL Orchestrator\n-> k9x HIL" as HIL
  rectangle "Model Router\n(eligibility, learned scores)" as MR
}

rectangle "AgentCore Gateway (Path C)\nCedar policy + Shield interceptor" as GW

rectangle "AgentCore Memory\n(session store)" as Mem
rectangle "Bedrock models\n(Converse API, BedrockLLM)" as Models
rectangle "Tools\n(MCP servers, APIs, Lambda)" as Tools

Client --> Router : AgentCore inbound JWT\n-> K9 principal
Router --> Orch : event_type A
Router --> Adapter : event_type B
Orch -[hidden]right-> Adapter
Shield -[hidden]right-> Gate

Orch --> Squad
Squad --> Agents

Adapter --> Harness : invoke

Harness ..> Gate : inline tool calls\ncome back to the adapter
Harness --> GW : server-side tools
Adapter ..> Shield : ingress, final output
Agents ..> Shield : governed by construction
Agents ..> MR : llm_invoke
Agents ..> Mem : sessions
Gate ..> HIL : review needed
Gate ..> Shield : tool args, results
MR --> Models
Gate --> Tools : allowed call
GW ..> Shield : every tool call and result
GW --> Tools : allowed by Cedar and Shield

note right of PB
  The adapter is one of the Router's
  orchestrators. The Harness takes the
  place of Squad -> Agent on this path.
  Harness inline-tool round trip:
  to be verified live.
  A deployed agent K9-AIF did not build
  is governed at its boundary only.
end note

note right of GW
  Cedar decides who may call which tool.
  Shield checks what the call carries:
  injection, PII, arguments against records.
  Covers agents in any framework.
end note
@enduml
